# PLACED — right-click the ground to put it down, and it keeps working by itself.
#
# WishPlaceTag drops an invisible marker armour stand facing the child, and this wrapper runs the
# effect from that marker on a fixed cadence. So `placed` means: a thing that sits there
# and does its effect to whatever comes near it — a trap, a campfire, a healing totem, a hatchery.
#
# WHY A PERIOD AND NOT EVERY TICK. A placed `hurt` firing twenty times a second is not a trap, it is
# a meat grinder that kills anything that brushes past before the child sees what happened; a placed
# `summon` on every tick fills the world in about four seconds. The cadence is what makes the class
# playable, so it is a real parameter rather than a constant.
#
# TARGET here is never @s — @s is the MARKER, an armour stand. An effect that lands on "you" lands
# on whoever is standing near the thing instead, which is what a placed healing totem should mean.
import common

reset
    /scoreboard objectives add mfam_place dummy
end

function give()
${GIVES}
    /tellraw @s {"text":"${GIVE_MESSAGE}","color":"${HEX}"}
end

clock tick
    /execute as @e[tag=${FEATURE}_here] run scoreboard players add @s mfam_place 1
    /execute as @e[tag=${FEATURE}_here,scores={mfam_place=${PERIOD_TICKS}..}] at @s run function $namespace:effect
    /execute as @e[tag=${FEATURE}_here,scores={mfam_place=${PERIOD_TICKS}..}] run scoreboard players set @s mfam_place 0
end

${EFFECT_BLOCK}
